---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/templates/editorial.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Diamond Education — The 4Cs, Shapes &amp; Anatomy | Bez Ambar"
  description="Master the fundamentals of diamond quality. Learn the 4Cs (cut, color, clarity, carat), diamond shapes, anatomy, and how to select your perfect stone. From the Bez Ambar atelier, Los Angeles."
  canonical="https://bezambar.com/diamond-education"
  headerLight={true}
>

<!-- Hero -->
<section class="de-hero">
  <p class="de-hero__eyebrow">Diamond Education</p>
  <h1 class="de-hero__title">The Language of Light</h1>
  <p class="de-hero__lede">Four characteristics determine a diamond's quality. Understanding them is the difference between buying a certificate and choosing a stone you will wear for a lifetime.</p>
</section>

<!-- Sticky tab navigation -->
<div class="ba-tab-bar" id="deTabs">
  <div class="ba-tab-bar__inner">
    <button class="ba-tab active" data-section="four-cs">The 4Cs</button>
    <button class="ba-tab" data-section="cut">Cut</button>
    <button class="ba-tab" data-section="color">Color</button>
    <button class="ba-tab" data-section="clarity">Clarity</button>
    <button class="ba-tab" data-section="carat">Carat</button>
    <button class="ba-tab" data-section="shapes">Shapes</button>
    <button class="ba-tab" data-section="anatomy">Anatomy</button>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- 4Cs Overview -->
<section class="de-section" id="four-cs">
  <div class="de-section__inner">
    <div class="de-section-header">
      <span class="de-eyebrow">Where to Begin</span>
      <h2 class="de-heading">The Four Cs</h2>
      <p class="de-intro">Diamond quality is universally measured by four characteristics. Each plays a distinct role in the stone's beauty. Understanding how they interact will help you find the right stone at the right price.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="de-four-cs">
      <div class="de-c-card">
        <div class="de-c-letter">C</div>
        <div class="de-c-body">
          <h3 class="de-c-name">Cut</h3>
          <p class="de-c-desc">How precisely the diamond is faceted. Determines how light enters, reflects, and exits. The most important of the four — a poor cut will dull even the finest stone.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-c-card">
        <div class="de-c-letter">C</div>
        <div class="de-c-body">
          <h3 class="de-c-name">Color</h3>
          <p class="de-c-desc">The absence of color in a white diamond. The GIA grades from D (colorless) to Z (light yellow). In the near-colorless range — G through J — color is invisible to the naked eye.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-c-card">
        <div class="de-c-letter">C</div>
        <div class="de-c-body">
          <h3 class="de-c-name">Clarity</h3>
          <p class="de-c-desc">The absence of internal inclusions and surface blemishes. Most are microscopic and invisible without magnification. Eye-clean stones at VS2 or SI1 are excellent value.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-c-card">
        <div class="de-c-letter">C</div>
        <div class="de-c-body">
          <h3 class="de-c-name">Carat</h3>
          <p class="de-c-desc">Weight, not size. One carat equals 200 milligrams. Larger stones are rarer, so price increases exponentially — a 2-carat stone of equal quality costs significantly more than twice a 1-carat.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Cut -->
<section class="de-section de-section--paper" id="cut">
  <div class="de-section__inner">
    <div class="de-section-header">
      <span class="de-eyebrow">The Most Important C</span>
      <h2 class="de-heading">Cut</h2>
      <p class="de-intro">Cut is not the shape of a diamond — it is the quality of its faceting. A diamond's ability to reflect light depends entirely on the precision of its proportions, symmetry, and polish. Two diamonds of identical color and clarity can look dramatically different if one is better cut.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="de-prose">
      <h3 class="de-subheading">What Cut Measures</h3>
      <p>The GIA evaluates cut on three dimensions: <strong>proportions</strong> — the relationship between table size, crown height, and pavilion depth; <strong>symmetry</strong> — how precisely the facets align; and <strong>polish</strong> — the condition of the surface at a microscopic level.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="de-grade-scale">
      <span class="de-scale-label">GIA Cut Grade Scale</span>
      <div class="de-grade-rows">
        <div class="de-grade-row">
          <div class="de-grade-name">Excellent</div>
          <div class="de-grade-bar-wrap"><div class="de-grade-bar" style="width:100%"></div></div>
          <div class="de-grade-desc">Maximum light reflection. Optimal proportions and polish. The standard we recommend.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-grade-row">
          <div class="de-grade-name">Very Good</div>
          <div class="de-grade-bar-wrap"><div class="de-grade-bar" style="width:80%"></div></div>
          <div class="de-grade-desc">Excellent light performance with minor proportional variations. Strong value.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-grade-row">
          <div class="de-grade-name">Good</div>
          <div class="de-grade-bar-wrap"><div class="de-grade-bar" style="width:60%"></div></div>
          <div class="de-grade-desc">Good light return but with more notable proportional differences.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-grade-row">
          <div class="de-grade-name">Fair</div>
          <div class="de-grade-bar-wrap"><div class="de-grade-bar" style="width:40%"></div></div>
          <div class="de-grade-desc">Moderate light return. Significant proportional compromise.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-grade-row">
          <div class="de-grade-name">Poor</div>
          <div class="de-grade-bar-wrap"><div class="de-grade-bar" style="width:20%"></div></div>
          <div class="de-grade-desc">Minimal light reflection. Avoid unless budget is the only consideration.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Cut pull quote -->
<div class="de-pull-quote">
  <p class="de-pull-quote__text">&ldquo;A well-cut diamond of modest color and clarity will outshine a poorly cut stone with a superior certificate.&rdquo;</p>
  <span class="de-pull-quote__attr">Bez Ambar &mdash; Los Angeles Atelier</span>
</div>

<!-- Color -->
<section class="de-section" id="color">
  <div class="de-section__inner">
    <div class="de-section-header">
      <span class="de-eyebrow">Colorless to Light</span>
      <h2 class="de-heading">Color</h2>
      <p class="de-intro">In white diamonds, value increases with the absence of color. The GIA scale runs from D — perfectly colorless — to Z, where a faint yellow is visible to the naked eye. The difference between adjacent grades is subtle; the difference between D and J is not.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="de-color-groups">
      <div class="de-color-group">
        <div class="de-color-swatches">
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--colorless"><span>D</span></div>
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--colorless"><span>E</span></div>
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--colorless"><span>F</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-color-group-label">Colorless</div>
        <div class="de-color-group-note">Rarest. No color detectable under any conditions.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-color-group">
        <div class="de-color-swatches">
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--near"><span>G</span></div>
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--near"><span>H</span></div>
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--near"><span>I</span></div>
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--near"><span>J</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-color-group-label">Near Colorless</div>
        <div class="de-color-group-note">Color not visible to the naked eye. Excellent value range.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-color-group">
        <div class="de-color-swatches">
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--faint"><span>K</span></div>
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--faint"><span>L</span></div>
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--faint"><span>M</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-color-group-label">Faint</div>
        <div class="de-color-group-note">Slight warmth detectable by a trained eye.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-color-group">
        <div class="de-color-swatches">
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--vlight"><span>N&ndash;R</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-color-group-label">Very Light</div>
        <div class="de-color-group-note">Color visible to the naked eye.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-color-group">
        <div class="de-color-swatches">
          <div class="de-color-swatch de-color-swatch--light"><span>S&ndash;Z</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-color-group-label">Light</div>
        <div class="de-color-group-note">Noticeable color. Significantly more affordable.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="de-prose">
      <h3 class="de-subheading">Fancy Colored Diamonds</h3>
      <p>Beyond the standard scale, diamonds can display intense yellows, pinks, blues, and greens. These <em>fancy colored</em> diamonds are graded separately and prized for the strength and purity of their hue — the opposite logic of the standard white diamond scale.</p>
      <p><strong>Our recommendation:</strong> For white diamonds, the G&ndash;J range offers exceptional beauty without color visible to the naked eye, at a significant price advantage over D&ndash;F.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Clarity -->
<section class="de-section de-section--paper" id="clarity">
  <div class="de-section__inner">
    <div class="de-section-header">
      <span class="de-eyebrow">Inclusions &amp; Blemishes</span>
      <h2 class="de-heading">Clarity</h2>
      <p class="de-intro">Nearly all diamonds contain minute inclusions — tiny crystals, feathers, or clouds formed during the stone's growth. Clarity measures how few and how minor these imperfections are. For most buyers, the objective is <em>eye-clean</em>: no inclusions visible at normal viewing distance without magnification.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="de-clarity-scale">
      <div class="de-clarity-row">
        <div class="de-clarity-grade">FL</div>
        <div class="de-clarity-right">
          <div class="de-clarity-name">Flawless</div>
          <div class="de-clarity-desc">No inclusions or blemishes under 10&times; magnification. Exceedingly rare.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-clarity-row">
        <div class="de-clarity-grade">IF</div>
        <div class="de-clarity-right">
          <div class="de-clarity-name">Internally Flawless</div>
          <div class="de-clarity-desc">No internal inclusions. Minor surface features only. Very rare.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-clarity-row">
        <div class="de-clarity-grade">VVS1&ndash;2</div>
        <div class="de-clarity-right">
          <div class="de-clarity-name">Very Very Slightly Included</div>
          <div class="de-clarity-desc">Minute inclusions barely detectable under magnification by a skilled grader.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-clarity-row">
        <div class="de-clarity-grade">VS1&ndash;2</div>
        <div class="de-clarity-right">
          <div class="de-clarity-name">Very Slightly Included</div>
          <div class="de-clarity-desc">Minor inclusions visible under magnification. Virtually always eye-clean.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-clarity-row">
        <div class="de-clarity-grade">SI1&ndash;2</div>
        <div class="de-clarity-right">
          <div class="de-clarity-name">Slightly Included</div>
          <div class="de-clarity-desc">Inclusions visible under magnification. SI1 is usually eye-clean; SI2 sometimes is.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-clarity-row">
        <div class="de-clarity-grade">I1&ndash;3</div>
        <div class="de-clarity-right">
          <div class="de-clarity-name">Included</div>
          <div class="de-clarity-desc">Inclusions visible to the naked eye. May affect brilliance and durability.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="de-prose">
      <h3 class="de-subheading">Common Inclusion Types</h3>
      <p><strong>Crystals</strong> — tiny mineral crystals trapped during formation. <strong>Feathers</strong> — internal fractures. <strong>Clouds</strong> — clusters of minute particles creating a hazy zone. <strong>Needles</strong> — thin, rod-like inclusions. <strong>Pinpoints</strong> — very small crystals, often appearing as dots.</p>
      <p><strong>Our recommendation:</strong> VS2 or SI1 for best value — the vast majority of stones in these grades are eye-clean, and the premium for FL or IF rarely translates into visible difference.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Carat -->
<section class="de-section" id="carat">
  <div class="de-section__inner">
    <div class="de-section-header">
      <span class="de-eyebrow">Weight &amp; Rarity</span>
      <h2 class="de-heading">Carat</h2>
      <p class="de-intro">Carat measures weight, not size. One carat equals 200 milligrams. A diamond's visual size also depends on its cut and shape — a well-cut stone will often appear larger than a poorly cut stone of the same weight.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="de-carat-stats">
      <div class="de-carat-stat">
        <div class="de-carat-stat__weight">0.5 ct</div>
        <div class="de-carat-stat__mm">~5.2 mm diameter</div>
        <div class="de-carat-stat__note">Half carat. Popular for accent stones and petite engagement rings.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-carat-stat">
        <div class="de-carat-stat__weight">1.0 ct</div>
        <div class="de-carat-stat__mm">~6.5 mm diameter</div>
        <div class="de-carat-stat__note">The benchmark carat weight. Strong demand means premium pricing at this threshold.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-carat-stat">
        <div class="de-carat-stat__weight">1.5 ct</div>
        <div class="de-carat-stat__mm">~7.4 mm diameter</div>
        <div class="de-carat-stat__note">A noticeable step up. Typically costs more than double a comparable 1.0 ct stone.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-carat-stat">
        <div class="de-carat-stat__weight">2.0 ct</div>
        <div class="de-carat-stat__mm">~8.2 mm diameter</div>
        <div class="de-carat-stat__note">Substantial presence. Rare at high quality; price escalates sharply.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="de-prose">
      <h3 class="de-subheading">The Exponential Price Relationship</h3>
      <p>Price does not scale linearly with weight. Larger stones are exponentially rarer, so a 2-carat diamond of comparable quality costs three to four times the price of a 1-carat. A well-cut 1.2-carat at VS1 may be a wiser and more beautiful choice than a 1.5-carat at SI2 for the same budget.</p>
      <h3 class="de-subheading">Just Below Key Weights</h3>
      <p>A diamond weighing 0.98 carats will appear nearly identical to a 1.0 carat stone — and may cost 20&ndash;30% less. The same logic applies at 1.48 vs 1.5, and 1.98 vs 2.0. These are among the practical strategies our clients use to maximize stone quality within budget.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Shapes -->
<section class="de-section de-section--paper" id="shapes">
  <div class="de-section__inner">
    <div class="de-section-header">
      <span class="de-eyebrow">Outline &amp; Character</span>
      <h2 class="de-heading">Diamond Shapes</h2>
      <p class="de-intro">Shape is the outline of the stone. Each shape has distinct proportions, facet arrangements, and optical characteristics. Shape preference is personal — but each choice carries aesthetic and practical implications.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="de-shapes-grid">
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="38"/>
            <line x1="50" y1="12" x2="50" y2="88" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="2,3"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="50" x2="88" y2="50" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="2,3"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Round Brilliant</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">58 facets. Maximum light return. The classic standard.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M50 15 L85 50 L50 85 L15 50 Z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Princess</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Invented by Bez Ambar. Square, brilliant-cut. Modern and architectural.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <ellipse cx="50" cy="50" rx="40" ry="28"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Oval</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Elongates the finger. Brilliant-cut. High fire and scintillation.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M50 18 L72 30 L80 50 L72 70 L50 82 L28 70 L20 50 L28 30 Z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Cushion</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Square with rounded corners. Romantic and soft. Strong dispersion.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="22" y="28" width="56" height="44" rx="2"/>
            <line x1="22" y1="38" x2="78" y2="38" stroke-width="0.5"/>
            <line x1="22" y1="62" x2="78" y2="62" stroke-width="0.5"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Emerald</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Step-cut. Rectangular facets create a hall-of-mirrors effect. Sophisticated.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M50 85 L20 28 Q35 12 50 14 Q65 12 80 28 Z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Pear</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Brilliant-cut teardrop. Feminine and distinctive.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M50 18 L82 50 L50 82 L18 50 Z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Marquise</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Elongated boat shape. Maximizes carat face-up. Bold and striking.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M22 28 L50 22 L78 28 L84 50 L78 72 L50 78 L22 72 L16 50 Z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Asscher</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Step-cut square. Art Deco origin. Deep, geometric facets.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M22 26 L50 20 L78 26 L82 50 L78 74 L50 80 L22 74 L18 50 Z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Radiant</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Brilliant-cut rectangle. High sparkle. Combines emerald shape with round brilliance.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M50 15 L72 35 L75 50 L50 82 L25 50 L28 35 Z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Blaze&reg;</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Bez Ambar proprietary. Patented faceting for maximum light dispersion.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="de-shape">
        <div class="de-shape__visual">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M50 20 Q68 20 75 35 Q82 50 50 82 Q18 50 25 35 Q32 20 50 20 Z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="de-shape__name">Heart</div>
        <div class="de-shape__note">Brilliant-cut. Romantic. Requires skilled symmetry to look balanced.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="de-prose">
      <h3 class="de-subheading">Shape vs. Cut</h3>
      <p>Shape and cut are distinct. Shape is the outline; cut is the quality of faceting. An oval can be Excellent or Poor cut — the shape does not determine the cut grade. All shapes can be cut to maximize their optical performance.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Anatomy -->
<section class="de-section" id="anatomy">
  <div class="de-section__inner">
    <div class="de-section-header">
      <span class="de-eyebrow">Structure &amp; Proportion</span>
      <h2 class="de-heading">Diamond Anatomy</h2>
      <p class="de-intro">The terms below define the parts of a diamond that determine its light performance. Understanding them helps you read a GIA certificate and understand why proportions matter.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="de-anatomy">
      <div class="de-anatomy__diagram">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 400" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <path d="M160 36 L248 128 L260 196 L160 356 L60 196 L72 128 Z" stroke="#1a1a1a" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <line x1="100" y1="36" x2="220" y2="36" stroke="#1a1a1a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="60" y1="196" x2="260" y2="196" stroke="#95826b" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
          <line x1="72" y1="128" x2="248" y2="128" stroke="#95826b" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3,3"/>
          <line x1="160" y1="36" x2="160" y2="356" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
          <line x1="220" y1="36" x2="272" y2="22" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="0.75"/>
          <text x="276" y="25" font-size="12" fill="#888" font-family="var(--sans)">Table</text>
          <line x1="248" y1="82" x2="272" y2="74" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="0.75"/>
          <text x="276" y="77" font-size="12" fill="#888" font-family="var(--sans)">Crown</text>
          <line x1="260" y1="196" x2="272" y2="196" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="0.75"/>
          <text x="276" y="199" font-size="12" fill="#888" font-family="var(--sans)">Girdle</text>
          <line x1="240" y1="268" x2="272" y2="276" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="0.75"/>
          <text x="276" y="279" font-size="12" fill="#888" font-family="var(--sans)">Pavilion</text>
          <line x1="163" y1="356" x2="272" y2="346" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="0.75"/>
          <text x="276" y="349" font-size="12" fill="#888" font-family="var(--sans)">Culet</text>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <dl class="de-anatomy__terms">
        <div class="de-term">
          <dt class="de-term__name">Table</dt>
          <dd class="de-term__def">The large flat facet on the very top of the diamond. Light enters primarily through the table; its size as a percentage of total width is a key cut quality indicator.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="de-term">
          <dt class="de-term__name">Crown</dt>
          <dd class="de-term__def">The upper portion between the table and the girdle. Crown facets bend incoming light to create the stone's fire and scintillation.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="de-term">
          <dt class="de-term__name">Girdle</dt>
          <dd class="de-term__def">The widest point of the diamond — the boundary between crown and pavilion. Sets the stone's diameter. Graded from extremely thin to extremely thick.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="de-term">
          <dt class="de-term__name">Pavilion</dt>
          <dd class="de-term__def">The lower portion below the girdle. Pavilion facets act as mirrors, reflecting light back up through the crown. Pavilion depth and angle are critical to brilliance.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="de-term">
          <dt class="de-term__name">Culet</dt>
          <dd class="de-term__def">The very bottom of the diamond. On modern stones, ideally a sharp point or a very small facet. A large culet was common in antique cuts and appears as a dark circle when viewed face-up.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="de-measurements">
      <h3 class="de-subheading">Key Proportions for Round Brilliants</h3>
      <div class="de-measure-grid">
        <div class="de-measure-item">
          <div class="de-measure-param">Depth %</div>
          <div class="de-measure-ideal">58&ndash;62%</div>
          <div class="de-measure-note">Total depth as percentage of diameter. Outside this range, light leaks or becomes trapped.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-measure-item">
          <div class="de-measure-param">Table %</div>
          <div class="de-measure-ideal">52&ndash;62%</div>
          <div class="de-measure-note">Table width as percentage of diameter. Affects balance between brilliance and fire.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-measure-item">
          <div class="de-measure-param">Crown Angle</div>
          <div class="de-measure-ideal">34&ndash;35&deg;</div>
          <div class="de-measure-note">Angle of crown facets. Controls dispersion of light and fire intensity.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="de-measure-item">
          <div class="de-measure-param">Pavilion Angle</div>
          <div class="de-measure-ideal">40&ndash;41&deg;</div>
          <div class="de-measure-note">Angle of pavilion facets. Determines the primary path of light reflection.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="ba-cta--paper ba-cta">
  <span class="ba-cta__eyebrow">The Collection</span>
  <h2 class="ba-cta__title">Diamonds Chosen for Their Character of Light</h2>
  <p class="ba-cta__body">Every stone in the collection is selected for what it does with light &mdash; not for its certificate alone. View the collection online, or by private appointment at the Los Angeles atelier.</p>
  <a href="/collection" class="ba-cta__btn">Discover the Collection</a>
</section>

</Layout>

